## Marrow Bay Free Library

::bg{location="library_reading_room" time="afternoon"}
::music{action="start" mood="peaceful" volume="down"}
@narrator: The library used to be a customs house. The counters where men weighed contraband now hold returned paperbacks, swollen with sea air.
::auto{character="ines" anchor="center" action="fadeInUp"}
::set{run.seen.ines = run.day}
@ines{emotion="neutral"}: We close at five. And you're dripping on the atlas.
@sol: Sorry. Pell sent me. She said you know about paper?
@ines{emotion="surprised"}: Pell Arden sent someone to me? On purpose?
@ines{emotion="shy"}: I mean. Yes. I know about paper. I know too much about paper, according to everyone.

<branch id="inesFirst" prompt="Ines is holding a book to her chest like a shield.">
  <choice id="ask" label="“Then tell me everything.”">
    ::set{run.aff.ines += 1}
    @ines{emotion="happy"}: Mulberry. Kozo, if you can get it. It's long-fibred, so it holds when it's wet — the water gets in between the fibres instead of breaking them.
    @ines{emotion="shy"}: …That was a lot. Sorry.
  </choice>
  <choice id="brief" label="“Just the short version.”">
    @ines{emotion="neutral"}: Don't use printer paper. It dies in the sea.
  </choice>
</branch>

@ines: The good sheets come with the Wednesday delivery. Come back Wednesday afternoon and I'll put some aside.
::auto{character="ines" action="fadeOut"}
@sol{mono}: Wednesday afternoon. I should write that down.
